		"habit": "a mature plant is 10 to 15 m tall and 3 to 5 m wide across its arms; height to width about 3 to 1. One trunk 30 to 75 cm thick, no crown; the whole height is stem. Widest at the arms, at about half the height. Outline: a candelabrum column. One stem, never branched at the ground.",
		"branching": "arms appear after 50 to 100 years. Two to six arms leave the trunk singly, at about one third to one half of the height, from a pinched junction. Each arm runs out nearly level for 0.3 to 1 m, bends at an elbow and rises parallel to the trunk to a rounded tip. One order only: arms do not branch again, or rarely.",
